{"title":"Career Roadmap — Sports Data Analyst","role":"Sports Data Analyst","summary":"A Sports Data Analyst uses statistics, programming, data visualization, and domain knowledge to convert sports data into insights that improve player performance, team strategy, scouting, recruitment, injury prevention, and business decisions.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Sports Engineering / Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Sports Data Analyst uses statistics, programming, data visualization, and domain knowledge to convert sports data into insights that improve player performance, team strategy, scouting, recruitment, injury prevention, and business decisions."},{"type":"p","text":"The role can combine:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sports statistics"},{"text":"Player-performance analytics"},{"text":"Match analysis"},{"text":"Biomechanics data"},{"text":"Wearable/sensor data"},{"text":"Video analytics"},{"text":"Scouting analytics"},{"text":"Team strategy"},{"text":"Sports business analytics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For a Sports Engineering / Technology graduate, the strongest positioning is Sports Analytics + Data Science + Sports Technology, rather than general business analytics."},{"type":"h","text":"Major employers:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Professional sports teams"},{"text":"Cricket franchises"},{"text":"Football clubs"},{"text":"Sports-tech companies"},{"text":"Sports analytics companies"},{"text":"Sports broadcasting companies"},{"text":"Sports academies"},{"text":"Fitness and wearable companies"},{"text":"Sports research laboratories"},{"text":"Sports federations"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Sports Data Analyst, Performance Analyst, Junior Sports Analyst"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Senior Sports Analy