ions in sports."},{"text":"Create clear data-driven recommendations."},{"text":"Present findings to coaches, analysts, or business stakeholders."},{"text":"Complete 3–5 sports analytics projects."},{"text":"Maintain a GitHub/portfolio showcasing sports analytics work."},{"text":"Obtain at least one sports-tech, sports analytics, data science, or performance-analysis internship."}]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The strongest profile for this career is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Sports Analytics","Statistics","Python/SQL","Machine Learning","Visualization","Sports Technology"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"For a Sports Engineering graduate, the competitive advantage comes from combining engineering/sensor knowledge with data science, rather than becoming only a conventional data analyst."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech Sports Engineering / Technology","Statistics + Python + SQL","Sports Performance Analytics","Machine Learning + Visualization","Tracking / Sensor / Video Analytics","Sports Analytics Internship","Sports Data Analyst","Senior Sports / Performance Analyst","Sports Data Scientist / Analytics Lead","Head of Sports Analytics","Sports Technology / Analytics Director"]},{"type":"flow","items":["Sports Statistics","Python","SQL","Power BI","Machine Learning","Computer Vision","Sensor/Tracking Analytics","Sports Domain Expertise."],"sep":"+","label":"Best-fit skill combination"}]}]}